  "id": "secondamendmentsuperstore",
  "neon": "#ff6a4a",
  "note": "SECOND AMENDMENT SUPERSTORE — the gun shop on Ironside Street, and the meanest object on it.\n\n⚠ THE MODEL IS BUILT TO THE TILE'S OWN PROSE RATHER THAN BESIDE IT. The room description has said\n\"a low blockhouse of riveted plate with a slit window and a door like a bank vault\" and quoted the\nboard over it — YOU BREAK THE GLASS, YOU MEET THE OWNER — for as long as the tile has existed, and\nthe generic armory arm drew a shop with a shutter. Both boards are here, and the window is a slit.\n\n⚠ IT IS THE LOWEST BUILDING ON THE STREET AND STAYS THAT WAY. A blockhouse gets its menace from\nbeing wide, windowless and close to the ground; make it tall and it is an office with a gun counter.\nThe only thing above the parapet is the range extension at the back, which is where the noise is.\n\n⚠ AND NOBODY HAS TAGGED IT. Every other frontage on this street carries a `tag`; this one\ndeliberately does not, and that absence is the single most characterful thing on the building.",
